The fix for crbug 584687200 (restricted: "Forbid CSSAnimations::Cancel during
animated style and update passes"): chromium/src main commit
35f4c4eaf5f2efda93f72f531fc7d003f22e6eb3 (main@{#1744462}), merged to the 159
branch as cee5956c35. 158's merge (Gerrit 8817167) was still pending as of
8127@{#1808}.

While Blink computes animated styles (StyleResolver::ApplyAnimatedStyle) or
applies pending animation and timeline updates
(PostStyleUpdateScope::ApplyAnimations), it walks the flat tree and the
animation and timeline maps. A shadow root whose slot assignment was left dirty
could have it recalculated lazily from Node::AssignedSlot() during those walks,
which detaches unslotted subtrees and calls CSSAnimations::Cancel(), clearing
the maps while they are being iterated: memory corruption in the renderer,
reachable from web content. The fix tracks both passes in StyleEngine and
CHECKs in CSSAnimations::Cancel() that neither is active.

This is the main commit's change without its test (css_animations_test.cc),
regenerated against 158's files (the .64 tree) so it applies without offsets;
the hunks are the same as main's, and the patched files are byte-identical to
those of the pending 158 merge's current patchset (cf21562c). Drop this once
158 gets the fix (check that the merged change is the same).

